Z:Source-assisted manual SATB transcription; no new harmony or tempo
N:All five printed stanzas, refrain, and all four source voice streams retained; final bass octave is a two-note chord.
N:Same Owens/Kirkpatrick hymn as catalog Will Your Anchor Hold - Piano; traditional vocal edition, no recording-arrangement match claimed.
N:Printed ties retained where alternate stanzas split syllables across tied notes; performance articulation is verse-dependent.
N:The source splits the fermata phrase ending and following pickup with separate barlines; those partial bars are retained.
N:Printed stanza 4 reads "On the rising tide it the never fail"; the apparent source typo is retained without silent correction.
N:Two lower-staff slurs in source system 2 have coincident paths; both voice slurs are retained.
N:Source Public Domain assertion retained; no worldwide or recording-specific rights clearance claimed.
N:Recommended-copy editorial correction: verse1 can->the, verse4 the->can, verse3 missing our restored at existing continuation slot; verified Winning Songs1892 p165. Canonical source transcription remains literal.
